        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U1 TPS62933 ... bucks +24V → +5V ... Powers ESP32 DevKit ... Feeds U2 (AZ1117-3.3 LDO) (§3)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The buck may remain disabled, leaving the +5 V rail without its intended supply and consequently depriving the ESP32 and downstream 3.3 V regulator of power.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["PR3", "H8", "P6"],
      "pins": ["PR3.1 (VCC)", "PR3.2 (SDA)", "PR3.3 (SCL)", "PR3.4 (GND)", "PR3.5", "PR3.6"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0009 (I2C_SDA)", "NET0039 (I2C_SCL)", "GND"],
      "observed": "The LiDAR symbol PR3 is wired through H8/P6: its VCC, SDA, SCL, and GND pins connect to supply, I2C, and ground nets.",
      "expected": "The specification says the TF-Luna LiDAR is not wired in this revision and that all of its pins are free.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "PR3 LiDAR pins VCC, SDA, SCL, and GND are wired to P6/H8 and the +5V, NET0009, NET0039, and GND connections (sheet 1, page 1)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... and all four pins ... typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net (§4.3)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The drawing implements a powered LiDAR/I2C interface that the stated design says is unwired; this changes the board's sensor connectivity and may place an additional device on the I2C bus.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The TPS62933 enable pin is explicitly left unconnected, putting the intended 5 V supply at risk. The drawing also wires a LiDAR interface despite the specification describing the LiDAR as unwired."
}

